{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Your princes. Companions.</b> From the root שלם ישלם (Exodus 22:4). The meaning: they would pervert justice, and the judge would say, give me such-and-such, and I will repay you the recompense in your judging against your fellow:" "<b>Orphan.</b> Because they do not fear him, they do not do him justice:" "<b>And the widow's cause.</b> If she has one, they do not wish to hear it, therefore it does not reach them:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Verse citation normalized from (שמות כ\"ב ה') to Exodus 22:4, following the Hebrew chapter-verse numbering which differs from English at this verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:46.052290519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}